cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FlowGuard++: Flow-Matching Query Monitoring Against Model Extraction"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
license: MIT

# TODO(release): replace every REPLACE_ME below with real values before tagging
# v1.0.0. GitHub renders this file as a "Cite this repository" button, and
# Zenodo reads it verbatim when it mints the DOI — errors here propagate into
# other people's bibliographies.
authors:
  - family-names: "REPLACE_ME"
    given-names: "REPLACE_ME"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    affiliation: "REPLACE_ME"
    email: "REPLACE_ME@example.org"

repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE_ME/flowguard"
url: "https://github.com/REPLACE_ME/flowguard"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-31"

abstract: >-
  FlowGuard++ is a query-level defense against black-box model-extraction
  attacks on machine-learning-as-a-service APIs. It scores incoming queries with
  a continuous normalizing flow trained by flow matching and fuses that
  per-query signal with stateful, per-client signals — a trajectory-integral
  velocity score, a Kolmogorov-Smirnov test over a sliding score window, and an
  MMD test on the client's label histogram. The repository also provides a
  reproducible benchmark of extraction attacks and prediction-perturbation
  defenses, including adaptive attacks with white-box access to the detector.

keywords:
  - model extraction
  - model stealing
  - machine learning security
  - flow matching
  - continuous normalizing flows
  - out-of-distribution detection
  - MLaaS

